---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy. Nomoro" description="What Nomoro collects, and what it doesn’t.">
  <section class="wrap pt-12 pb-24 lg:pt-24 lg:pb-40">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <div class="lg:col-start-3 lg:col-span-7 flex flex-col gap-6 body">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1 class="h1">What we collect, and what we don’t.</h1>
        <p class="body-l pt-4">Less data is part of less to do.</p>
        <h2 class="h3 pt-6">Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use Plausible, a privacy focused analytics service hosted in the EU. It counts page views without
          cookies and without collecting personal data. There is no consent banner because there is nothing to
          consent to.
        </p>
        <h2 class="h3 pt-6">The letter</h2>
        <p>
          If you subscribe, we store your email address with our newsletter provider in order to send you the
          Nomoro letter. You can unsubscribe with one click in any email, and your address is deleted when you
          do. We never sell or share it.
        </p>
        <h2 class="h3 pt-6">Observations and email</h2>
        <p>
          When you write to us, we keep your message to reply to it. If we quote an observation in the journal,
          we ask first and credit you only if you want us to.
        </p>
        <h2 class="h3 pt-6">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under the GDPR you can ask what we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted. Write to
          <a href="mailto:hello@nomoro.be" class="link">hello@nomoro.be</a>. The controller is Nomoro BV,
          Westerlo, Belgium.
        </p>
        <p class="small text-steel pt-6">Last updated November 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
